### NAASCO Audit API Tests
### Make sure the server is running on http://localhost:3001

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001
@token = YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 1. Get all audit logs (with pagination)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/audit
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2. Get audit logs with filters
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/audit?action=CREATE&entityType=user&page=1&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. Get audit logs by date range
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/audit?startDate=2024-01-01&endDate=2024-12-31
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Get specific audit log by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/audit/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Get audit logs for specific entity
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/audit/entity/user/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Get audit logs for specific user
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/audit/user/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 7. Get audit statistics (last 30 days)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/audit/stats
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. Get audit statistics (last 7 days)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/audit/stats?days=7
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. Get available audit actions
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/audit/actions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Get available entity types
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/audit/entity-types
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 11. Filter by multiple criteria
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/audit?userId=1&action=UPDATE&entityType=user&startDate=2024-01-01
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 12. Test pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/audit?page=2&limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 13. Filter by specific user and date range
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/audit?userId=2&startDate=2024-06-01&endDate=2024-12-31
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
